###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - RFF, O-RFF and RFM are encoded as one registry method (random-feature potential); the orthogonal variant and the descriptor order are settings. RFM uses a different feature map (for SOAP-type descriptors) than RFF; if they should be two methods, the diamond run moves to a second registry row.
# - The GAP baselines here use two-body or three-body descriptors only, while the registry label of entity:GAP still says 'with SOAP kernel' (legacy label, listed for generalisation in METHODS.md).
# - Reference levels, sizes and splits of the libatoms.org data sets are not restated in the paper and are not encoded. The graphene in-plane and out-of-plane force RMSEs (0.070 and 0.044 eV/A), the tungsten RFM model (errors only in figures), learning curves and the physical properties of Table 3 (lattice constants, elastic constants, phonons) are not encoded. Training times are in seconds and kept in comments because mlips:trainingDuration is in hours.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

